WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.040
-This spring, see the story
of the black woman who became

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:11.043
a world-renowned scientist,
an accomplished cellist,

00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:12.879
and activist,

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:16.883
and a man who was white
while she did it.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:20.053
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:22.755
-Her mic was too high,
but I fixed it.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.425
It's fixed because of me.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:29.329
[ Whispers ]
You're doing great.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.997
-"White Savior."

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.999
It's about all the things
white people love

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.667
in movies about racism,

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.235
like that scene
where they're in the bar

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:38.671
and the white person sticks up
for the black person.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.274
-This bar don't serve
people like you.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.242
-I have just as much a right
to be here --

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:44.544
-Hey...

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.646
she's with me.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.882
-Oh! Sorry about that, Jack.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.216
-That's all right, bubba.
How are the kids?

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.317
-Good.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.584
They're good.
-Good.

00:00:52.584 --> 00:00:54.254
Good.
-Great.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.788
[ Laughter ]
-That thing where

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:58.224
a white person works closely
with a black person

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.560
and is surprised
to learn they're smart.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.061
-Oh, my God.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:03.396
You did it.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.898
-Well, I've always been
pretty good at math.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:08.334
-Well, you should go
to school for it.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.003
-I did.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.704
-You should get a job in it.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.773
-I have one.
-You do?

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:14.841
Where?

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.010
-Here.
I'm your boss.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.711
-You?!

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:21.514
[ Chuckles ] Wow.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.016
-Now clean this up
and get me a coffee.

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.219
-No.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.221
-There's also the part
where the black person

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.390
very calmly eviscerates
a white person

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.257
in a way that makes
white audiences think,

00:01:32.257 --> 00:01:34.360
that was the day
racism was solved,

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.895
and makes black audiences think,

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.964
"I had to do that same [bleep]
last week."

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:40.266
Don't forget the part

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:45.170
where the black person
bravely defies racist laws.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:46.806
And then the white guy steps in

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.142
like he's some sort
of Goddamn hero.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.276
-You should be ashamed
of yourselves, lady.

00:01:51.276 --> 00:01:52.679
You know,
it's people like you --

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:55.481
-I can't go with you
standing up there are.

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:56.983
-Oh, okay.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.652
-And one racist who's
so cartoonishly racist

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.754
that other racists
watch this movie and say,

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.923
"Well, at least,
I'm not that racist."

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:08.394
-Well, well, well,
look at what we have here.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.930
If it ain't another
gobbedy-goo-goo

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.765
ga-ga-goo-goo-ga-doodle.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.934
A gaga-gaga-gogle!

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.469
[ Barks ]

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:20.106
[ Barking continues ]

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:22.475
[ Speak gibberish ]

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.714
From the makers of
"Green Book," "Hidden Figures,"

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:30.316
"The Help," "The Blind Side,"

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.352
"Dangerous Minds," "Glory,"
"Cool Runnings,"

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.587
"Radio," "Hard Ball,"
"Ghosts of Mississippi,"

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.255
"The Principal,"
"A Time to Kill,"

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:37.823
"Freedom Riders,"
"Sunset Park,"

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:41.728
"The Air Up There"
and "Wild Cats."

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.930
-Hey, thanks for everything.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.264
-You're welcome.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:48.501
[ Chuckling ] Now, don't you go
falling in love with me.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.003
-I won't...

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:53.005
because that doesn't
test well with audiences.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.174
♪♪

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:58.143
-"People" magazine says,
"This movie is a triumph,"

00:02:58.143 --> 00:03:00.212
and the black person
it's based on says,

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:02.014
"This is not at all
how it happened,"

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:04.149
and if you're a black person
hoping for the catharsis

00:03:04.149 --> 00:03:06.118
of watching a black character
punch a racist,

00:03:06.118 --> 00:03:07.720
you'll get the next
best thing...

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.788
-[ Grunts ]

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.990
-...the white guy
punching a racist.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.491
-If I'd have done that,

00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:15.461
they'd have locked me up
until I died.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:18.264
-Plus, a scene where
the white guy is helpful

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.698
in a way that doesn't
advance the cause

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:21.333
of all black people...

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:23.169
just the one he's friends with.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:24.337
-Huh?

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:31.844
♪♪

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.879
-It also have stuff like this.

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:35.914
-I know what it's like for you.

00:03:35.914 --> 00:03:40.419
And there's nothing worse
than feeling like an outsider.

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:42.087
Like, one time...

00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:43.422
when I was in junior high,

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:47.126
I got some toilet paper stuck
to the bottom of my shoe,

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.461
and the other kids, well...

00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:51.530
you know how kids can be.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:54.100
They called me "Mr. Poop Shoe."

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.668
I felt like it
went on for weeks,

00:03:56.668 --> 00:04:01.040
but it was actually probably
only about five minutes

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.641
before someone told me,
and I took it off,

00:04:02.641 --> 00:04:05.411
but, yeah.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.080
I understand racism.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:11.650
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.853
-Featuring a scene
where the white character

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:16.222
introduces the black character
to something they definitely

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.657
already knew about.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:22.528
-I'm gonna teach you about
a little something called jazz.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.530
-And no "White Savior" movie
is complete

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.099
without a white woman
adopting a black person.

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:29.001
-I'm here to adopt you.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.736
-Adopt me?

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:32.038
I'm older than you.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:36.009
-You will no longer want
for anything in this world.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:38.544
-Word?

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:41.814
Bye, children!

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.283
Hey, Mommy, what's for dinner?

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.084
-Well, I guess I'd have
to ask the chef.

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.986
-Chef?!

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.788
-Some movies examine
the complexities

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.723
of race relations in America.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.558
This movie does not do that.

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:53.726
But according to "The Root,"

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.561
it does push a black
helplessness narrative

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.431
that paints black people as
passive in their own history.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:00.165
Plus it's corny.

00:05:00.165 --> 00:05:02.402
And you know this movie was
written by a white person

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.470
because the black person
becomes friends

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.838
with the racist.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.974
-You know what, Loretta,
you're all right.

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:10.042
-Thanks, Earl.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:11.877
For some reason,
earning your respect

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:15.214
is something I'm interested in.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:18.250
-"White Savior."

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.986
In theaters this spring.

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.155
And coming soon,
the Rosa Parks story

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:24.089
told from the perspective
of a white guy

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:25.558
who was also on the bus --

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.893
"Rosa and Kevin."

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:35.735
♪♪

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:37.903
-Hey!

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.739
This seat's free.
[ Cheers and applause ]

